  "body": "PR #913 (PROCESS_VERSION 15) made `cargo xtask gate` use sccache by itself, but a plain `cargo test -p ...`, `cargo build` or `cargo clippy` only uses the cache when `RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache` is set in the shell, and nothing tells the agents so: the skills only say not to export `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`. Workers and reviewers that call cargo directly therefore build without the cache. Maintainer decision (2026-11-11): put the instruction in the shared files, and keep the release build out of the cache.\n\nDo:\n1. One short, identical line in `.claude/skills/work-issue/SKILL.md`, `.claude/skills/resolve-conflicts/SKILL.md`, `.claude/agents/PR-reviewer.md`, `.claude/agents/gate-runner.md` (and the `issue-worker-*` agents only if they carry build instructions of their own): prefer `cargo xtask gate ...` (it turns the cache on); for a direct cargo call, set `RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache` when `sccache` is on PATH (`command -v sccache`), never when it is not (cargo fails if the wrapper is missing); never export `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`. AGENTS.md's build-cache paragraph says the same in one sentence.\n2. `cargo xtask release` (`xtask/src/release.rs`, `build()`) builds the shipped binary WITHOUT a compiler wrapper even when `RUSTC_WRAPPER` is set in the environment (remove it from the child's environment), pinned by an xtask unit test. Reason: a maintainer may set `RUSTC_WRAPPER` machine-wide (this repo's maintainer has, in local Claude Code settings), and the released artifact must not depend on a compile cache. The release GATE tier may keep using the cache; only the packaging build clears it - say so in the code comment.\n3. Do NOT add `rustc-wrapper` to the checked-in `.cargo/config.toml` (cargo fails outright on a machine without sccache) and do not add it to the checked-in `.claude/settings.json` for the same reason.\n\nProcess files: bump `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` (16, or the next free number when it merges); the merge is announced on #681.\n\nDone means: the four files carry the line; AGENTS.md matches; the release packaging build ignores `RUSTC_WRAPPER`, pinned by a unit test; xtask's unit tests pass. Related: #900, #914, #915.\n",
